This is a open source repository. 
Fork this repo and create a branch then add your codes. 
1. I fork a public repo
2. Then I clone the forked repo to my laptop.
3. Work on the code changes on my local laptop.
4. Then I sync fork.
5. I git pull from the forked repo to get the changed files.
6. Then I git push -u origin fork-branch
7. Add the person who created the fork-branch as a collaborator in gh.com 
8. in gh.com create a pull request.
9. Compare and merge the pull request.

